# Copy to .env and fill in what you have. .env is gitignored. Never commit a real key.
#
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY REQUIRED, measured 2026-09-06 by disabling each one and re-running:
#
#   nothing          the PAGE renders. Every panel that cannot get its data says
#                    "unavailable" and names the fix, rather than going blank.
#   UNUSUALWHALES    REQUIRED for the weekly book to produce ANY card. Not optional.
#   ANTHROPIC        optional. Switches on the written commentary; nothing structural.
#   POLYGON          optional. Only 05_studies reads it.
#
# The previous version of this file said "None are required to render the dashboard",
# which is true of the page and badly misleading about the product. See below.

# ─── REQUIRED for the weekly options book ────────────────────────────────────────
# Same-day dealer gamma, classified flow lean, dark-pool buy share, short float, and
# insider open-market buys.
#
# WITHOUT THIS KEY THE WEEKLY BOOK PRODUCES ZERO CARDS, and that is by design rather
# than a bug. A card needs three distinct inputs agreeing (MIN_VOTING_INPUTS). Four of
# the seven possible voters come from this API:
#
#     flow_lean · dp_buy_share · short_float_pct · insider_open_buys
#
# The three that need no key are desk_macro, trend and vix_backwardation — and
# vix_backwardation ABSTAINS whenever the VIX term structure is in contango, which is
# most of the time. So without Unusual Whales the pool is usually just the macro read
# plus a moving average: two things, one of which is a transform of price. Measured on
# 2026-09-06 with the key disabled: 0 cards, 32 names refused for "too few inputs".
#
# A LAPSED subscription is not the same as a missing key: uw_client trips itself after
# repeated 401s and reports which of the two happened.
#
# NOTE ON QUOTA: the weekly universe is 103 names. Requiring a macro basis before the
# profile fetch keeps the calls to ~30 a cycle; removing that gate exhausted the daily
# limit mid-run and the vote silently degraded to trend-only.
UNUSUALWHALES_API_KEY=

# ─── OPTIONAL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The desk analyst, the trading agent, the committee, the lessons loop, and parsing a
# pasted desk note into the macro overlay. Without it each of those falls back to a
# rule-based path and says so. No trade card depends on it: the overlay can be written
# without a model, and every number on a card is computed in Python.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Minute bars for 05_studies only. The live dashboard never reads it. The free tier is
# reference data — no historical option or equity aggregates.
POLYGON_API_KEY=

# ─── NO KEY NEEDED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# yfinance is the workhorse and is unauthenticated: every price, option chain, strike
# ladder, bid/ask and expiry the weekly engine and the gap scanner use comes from it.
# It is rate-limited by politeness rather than by contract, so a 103-name scan takes
# about two minutes.
#
# squeezemetrics.com serves the prior-close gamma baseline as a free CSV, used as the
# fallback when Unusual Whales is unavailable.

# ─── PATHS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the ~26 live snapshots and the sqlite books are written. Defaults to
# <repo>/04_live_system/data.
# IDT_STATE_ROOT=/path/to/04_live_system/data

# The 16 GB of market data, which is NOT in git (06_data_guide/DATA.md). Only the
# backtests and 05_studies need it; the live dashboard works without it.
# IDT_DATA_ROOT=/path/to/index-daytrading/data

# Contact address sent to OpenAlex and the SEC, which both ask callers to identify
# themselves. Only needed for the literature and EDGAR scripts in 05_studies/.
CONTACT_EMAIL=
